From 23eb1212d09381e046dfc04d1d4088787bdd7874 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brandon Williams <turbine.bmw@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 09:43:25 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2143/2165] arm64: skip the EFI reset path when restarting from
 a panic in interrupt context

ResetSystem() runs EFI runtime services, which fault when invoked from
interrupt or atomic context (softlockup/hardlockup panic). On the Surface
Pro 11 the EFI reset from IRQ context oopses and wedges instead of
rebooting. Fall through to the PSCI restart handler in that case.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Brandon Williams <turbine.bmw@gmail.com>
(cherry picked from commit 69c3eec0bd1b0175ec2a002147358a900e94fa3b)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/kernel/process.c b/arch/arm64/kernel/process.c
index 581f80e9b9b730041f5653080b8cc0f7b37e4b75..6b2445b15571426ed7943538f7adbe5b91725028 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/kernel/process.c
+++ b/arch/arm64/kernel/process.c
@@ -135,9 +135,14 @@ void machine_restart(char *cmd)
 
 	/*
 	 * UpdateCapsule() depends on the system being reset via
-	 * ResetSystem().
+	 * ResetSystem().  However ResetSystem() runs EFI runtime services,
+	 * which fault if invoked from interrupt/atomic context (e.g. a
+	 * softlockup or hardlockup panic).  On such a panic, skip the EFI
+	 * reset and fall through to the PSCI restart handler, which resets
+	 * cleanly from any context.  (SP11/X1E80100: EFI reset from IRQ
+	 * context oopses and wedges instead of rebooting.)
 	 */
-	if (efi_enabled(EFI_RUNTIME_SERVICES))
+	if (efi_enabled(EFI_RUNTIME_SERVICES) && !in_interrupt() && !oops_in_progress)
 		efi_reboot(reboot_mode, NULL);
 
 	/* Now call the architecture specific reboot code. */
